<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Chocolatey package for anime-sh.

  Version and the installer's sha256 are placeholders, filled in by
  scripts/make_manifests.py from the built artifact. The same rule as the winget
  and scoop manifests: the two fields that must match an exact published file
  are never typed by hand.
-->
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>anime-sh</id>
    <version>0.0.0</version>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/Anime123450/anime-sh/tree/master/packaging/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <owners>Anime123450</owners>

    <title>anime-sh</title>
    <authors>Animesh Sharma</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/Anime123450/anime-sh</projectUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/Anime123450/anime-sh/blob/master/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/Anime123450/anime-sh</projectSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/Anime123450/anime-sh/blob/master/README.md</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/Anime123450/anime-sh/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/Anime123450/anime-sh/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md</releaseNotes>
    <tags>anime cli tui terminal streaming anilist mpv foss</tags>
    <summary>The terminal-native anime client - providers, mirrors and resolvers, handled for you.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
anime-sh finds a show, picks a working source and plays it in mpv, from the
terminal. It tracks what you have watched, resumes where you stopped, and can
sync progress with AniList. Sources are plugins, so a site going down does not
take the app with it.

### What gets installed

A single standalone executable with Python and every library inside it — there
is nothing to set up and no Python required.

**mpv** is installed alongside it (the `mpvio` package), because it is what
actually plays the video.

**ffmpeg** is *not* installed: it is needed only by `anime download`, and the
usual Windows build is several hundred megabytes. If you want downloads:

    choco install ffmpeg

Run `anime doctor` after installing and it will tell you what it found and what
is missing.
]]></description>

    <dependencies>
      <!--
        `mpvio`, not `mpv`. The package named `mpv` on the community repository
        is titled "[Deprecated] mpv" and its own description says it is
        deprecated in favour of `mpvio`; it is pinned to a 2024 build. `mpvio`
        is the one that follows upstream mpv's version scheme and is still
        published.

        Declared rather than bundled: mpv is GPL, so shipping its binary inside
        an MIT package would also make us responsible for offering its source.
      -->
      <!--
        The floor is the version actually tested against - on CI and locally -
        not the oldest that might work. chocolatey's validator asks for a
        minimum version, and the honest answer to "what do we support" is the
        one we have run. It is also the current release, so for anyone
        installing fresh this constrains nothing.
      -->
      <dependency id="mpvio" version="0.41.0" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
